docs/scratch/arrival-break/sol-s4-integration-r2-stdout.log:12926:The first raw-string shapes were safely refuse-shaped, which the contract explicitly permits. A stronger variant does cross the line: when a hash-raw backend property contains an embedded quote followed by `//`, the locator truncates inside the property, publish succeeds, and the unconsumed property bytes are silently reinterpreted as a comment. That is neither “refuse-shaped” nor a correct clause span; I’m pinning this accepting case as the blocker rather than treating safe refusal as a defect.
